Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||09-25-1999||02:29 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/fiero/fieropics/p-interior.jpg">  <P>I don't care much for the woodgrain dash stuff, or the analog gauges (digital!!) and it'd be cooler as a manual trans with a short shifter.. other than those minor details, that's probably the coolest interior I've ever seen.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>When I saw the image on Chris's page, I remembered I had a few images of this car as well, when the original Russian page was online for a little while.<BR>Regarding the rest of the car, any comments on the massive wing (tail??) on the back?<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 09-25-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000008||Clint||09-25-1999||03:00 PM||||Does anyone have any further info on This Bill person or his company before I call and pester? I was under the impression the Pyrahna wasn't made anymore.||||reg||5
Z||000009||Clint||09-25-1999||08:24 PM||||Well I called Bill. he sold the company 6 weeks ago. The companys phone number is 937-222-6444. They will be producing the american Pyrahna. BUT!!!  The car that many of us are referring to. (and the one that is pictured here in this thread) looks nothing like the american one. (there is a testorassa style) The one most of us are referring to (according to Bill) was built in Checkoslovia(sp?)  Bill said that it was just a dream.  The company built the one, took a bunch of money from people wanting to buy the kit and were never heard from again... VERY interesting.  Anyone else have any further info?  like is someone trying to make a kit similar?  Since it was only used to rip people off buy a checkslv. company i'm sure they have to legal rights to the design...<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000010||Clint||09-25-1999||08:26 PM||||sorry, that should say NO legal rights to the design.||||reg||1
